filenumber 632889
! STAGE 7 -- CONSTANT-RATE injection on corrected code.
! The run res911.in was meant to be. res911.in has three
! silent defects and cannot just be rerun:
!
!  1. IT NEVER INJECTED. injectionfromfile F + problem 3dp routes to
!     Beuler2d, whose constant-rate branch is commented out and marked
!     "No longer correct!" (m_diffusion.f90:677-680). Only the 1D
!     solvers still have it (:234, :347). No source term at all.
!  2. shear_mod is not a recognised key -- read_inputfile has only
!     case('rigid') (main_LH.f90:2695) -- so it ran at the default
!     rigid = 32.04 (m_const.f90:5), not the 24 it asked for.
!  3. Sw_fwid was absent and defaults to 1.0 (main_LH.f90:180) against
!     the 7.4e-9 in use, eight orders out. It sets the wellbore
!     coupling gamma (m_diffusion.f90:671) and divides the injection
!     term (:675, :763).
!
! Constant rate is delivered through the injection FILE path instead,
! which is tested and carries the Peaceman well model: const_rate_5.0e-03.txt holds
! two points with equal rates, and the interpolation holds the last
! value beyond the end (m_diffusion.f90:650-660), so the rate is
! exactly 5.0000e-03 throughout. june_clean.txt is untouched.
!
! imax/jmax 600 -> 601 so there IS an exact centre cell for the well;
! an even grid has no centre, which matters for comparison against an
! axisymmetric analytical solution.
!
! permev T -- res911.in's own setting, kp = kpmin growing toward
! kpmax. Paired with res632888.in so the effect of enhancement on the
! clean constant-rate problem is isolated. NOT the analytical case.
!
! kp RAISED from the parent's 1e-15 to 1.0e-13, and ds from 5 m to
! 20 m. This is not a preference -- the parent's value is
! COMPUTATIONALLY INFEASIBLE. Submitted verbatim as 632886/632887 it drove
! the adaptive timestep to 0.01 s and held it there: 252 million steps
! would have been needed to reach tmax against an nstep budget of 400000,
! stopping at 0.05 d of 30.66. Both were cancelled at step 240. A nearly
! impermeable medium under constant injection builds well pressure faster
! than the integrator can follow. The same tightness is on record giving
! 144 MPa of injector overpressure against sigmainit 30 (632510), which
! limitsigma T / minsig 1 would then clamp -- a nonlinearity no
! linear-diffusion solution contains.
!
! Domain: D = kp/(eta*phi*beta) = 0.4994 m^2/s, so the 30.66 d
! diffusion length is 2.30 km against a 6.010 km
! half-domain = 38%. At ds 5 m the half-domain would
! be 1.50 km and this would be 153% -- off the edge.
problem 3dp
imax 601
jmax 601
ds 0.02
interval 30
nstep 400000
tmax 0.08400000
dtmax 43200
dtout 0.0002
parameterfromfile F
backslip T
vpl 0d0
a 0.015
b 0.012
dc 1e-4
f0 0.6
muinit 0.37
sigmainit 30.0
velinit 1d-12
limitsigma T
minsig 1
velmin 1d-20
pressurediffusion T
permev T
kpmax 2.5e-13
kpmin 1.0e-13
kp 1.0e-13
phi 0.01
beta 2.25e-8
eta 0.89e-3
kL 1e-3
kT 1e15
pfinit 0d0
bcl Dirichlet
bcr Dirichlet
bct Dirichlet
bcb Dirichlet
pbcl 0d0
pbcr 0d0
pbct 0d0
pbcb 0d0
injectionfromfile T
injection_file "const_rate_5.0e-03.txt"
rigid 24
Sw_fwid 7.4e-9
rw 8.9e-2
